EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:

The applicant is requesting to amend the zoning map to change the zoning district for 4505 & 4435 Ridge
Road from NB- Neighborhood Business to CB- Community Business. The applicant desires to rezone the
subject property to redevelop and expand the existing commercial site and business. As proposed, the
existing station and car wash would be demolished and a new station constructed.

The existing gas station was constructed in 1977 and met the zoning ordinance standards of the time.
The station is currently oriented toward Ridge Road and is comprised of a 2,400 square foot convenience
store and one gas pump island with four fuel stations. A car wash was constructed in 1985 directly south
of the station but will not be reconstructed with the raze and rebuild project.

The proposed gas station would be reoriented toward Dell Range, and would include an approximately
6,466 square foot convenience store and four canopied gas pump islands. The proposal is anticipated to
meet or exceed all CB zoning requirements which will be reviewed during the Site Plan process. The
application will also include a proposal to modify property lines. This adjustment will be established
through the Administrative Plat process.

The requested zone change from NB to CB would allow for the redevelopment and reasonable expansion
of, and investment in, an existing commercial site and business. The current NB zoning designation would
make it difficult to construct a large-scale gas station that would both meet the required setbacks and
maintain appropriate circulation patterns within the site. Additionally, expansion of the gas station to
allow for four gas pump islands would not be permitted under the current NB zoning designation. The NB
zoning district permits up to two fuel pump islands with no more than eight fueling stations. Alternatively
the CB zoning district permits by right up to four fuel pump islands with no more than 16 fueling stations.

The proposed zone change is requested in order for the applicant to increase the number of fuel pumps,
and allow for site improvements for the convenience store. The CB district is a more typical zone along
the Dell Range corridor and is more conducive to larger commercial developments. The redevelopment of
the property as a gas station is appropriate. The property's location at the intersection of Dell Range and
Ridge, two major roadways is well suited for a gas station. This is proven by the fact that a viable station
has occupied the site for nearly 40 years. The gas station use would meet all standards as outlined in the
zoning ordinance and the redevelopment would aesthetically improve both the property and the
intersection.
```

### Page 6 of 9

```text
4

ZONE CHANGE DATA:  In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and decisions
on a proposed Zone Change Request, the Staff, Planning Commission and City Council shall use the
following criteria:

PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan.

Community Business is the designation given to the subject area within ShapeCheyenne, which
has the future land use map within PlanCheyenne. Community Business areas encourage a range
of retail and office uses to serve neighborhoods and the community and region, usually located at
the intersection of two major arterial roadways. Appropriate primary uses include supermarkets,
general retail, office and large tenant retail. The site is near properties zoned CB and
development trends and patterns in the area largely reflect CB development standards.

SURROUNDING AREA - The application is compatible with nearby property, specifically considering existing
zoning, the Comprehensive Plan, and any other official plans and policies created under the guidance of
that plan for these areas.

The existing zoning is NB Neighborhood Business. A designation of CB Community Business is
compatible with nearby property. As previously discussed, the CB Community Business zone
district is able to fit within the context of the Community Business future land use designation
and is therefore compatible with the comprehensive plan.

ZONING: BASIC STANDARDS & USES - The suitability of the subject property for development according to
the standards and uses of the existing zoning district, compared to the suitability of the subject property
for development according to the standards and uses of the proposed zoning district;

It would be challenging for the subject property to develop according to the standards and uses
of the existing zoning district. Under the proposed CB Community Business zone district, the
property would be able to be developed according to the standards of that district as laid out by
the Cheyenne UDC.

STREETS & OPEN SPACE - The ability of the subject property and surrounding vicinity to be developed
according to the Subdivision Standards in Article 4 considering the proposed zoning;

The property should be able to be developed according to the standards in Section 4 of the UDC.
Open Space will be further evaluated at the time of Site Plan Review, at which time any
requirements or exceptions thereto will be determined.

ZONING: INTENT, APPLICABILITY & DESIGN OBJECTIVES - The ability of the application to support the
Intent and Applicability statements of the proposed zoning district, and achieve the Design Objectives of
any specific standards.

The CB Community Business zone district is intended for Retail, Employment, Service and Civic
uses that may serve a number of residential neighborhoods or other districts. These uses should
```

